# Unreal Engine 5 Development Guide

This skill governs C++ and Blueprint architecture in **Unreal Engine 5 (UE 5.1 - 5.5)**.

## Core Architectural Patterns

### 1. C++ & Reflection Macro Discipline
- **Exposing Types to Reflection:**
  - Classes inheriting from `UObject` must have `UCLASS()`, `GENERATED_BODY()`.
  - Structs must use `USTRUCT(BlueprintType)` and member variables must have `UPROPERTY()`.
- **Property Specifiers:**
  - `UPROPERTY(EditDefaultsOnly, BlueprintReadOnly, Category = "Combat")`: Exposed on the Blueprint Class defaults, not editable per-instance in the level viewport.
  - `UPROPERTY(EditInstanceOnly, Category = "Level")`: Exposed only per placed level instance.
  - `UPROPERTY(VisibleAnywhere, BlueprintReadOnly)`: Read-only component pointers.
- **Function Specifiers:**
  - `UFUNCTION(BlueprintCallable)`: Callable from Blueprint event graphs.
  - `UFUNCTION(BlueprintPure)`: Side-effect free getter functions (no execution pins).
  - `UFUNCTION(BlueprintNativeEvent)` / `UFUNCTION(BlueprintImplementableEvent)`: For C++ default implementations that can be overridden in Blueprints (`_Implementation` postfix in C++).

### 2. Memory & Garbage Collection Management
- **`UObject` Pointers:**
  - Raw `UObject*` variables MUST be marked with `UPROPERTY()` or wrapped in smart pointers; otherwise, the garbage collector will sweep them unexpectedly, resulting in dangling pointers and fatal crashes.
  - Use `TWeakObjectPtr<T>` when referencing an actor or object that you do not own to avoid keeping it alive during level changes.
  - For non-`UObject` C++ classes, use `TSharedPtr<T>` and `TUniquePtr<T>`.

### 3. Gameplay Framework Role Separation
- `AGameModeBase`: Server-authoritative rules, win/loss conditions, spawn logic.
- `APlayerController`: Non-physical representation of the human player, input routing, UI management, RPC handlers.
- `APawn` / `ACharacter`: Physical in-world avatar (mesh, collisions, movement components).
- `APlayerState`: Persistent player state (score, ping, player stats) across actor respawns.
- `UActorComponent`: Reusable, modular gameplay behaviors (e.g. `HealthComponent`, `InventoryComponent`) attached to actors rather than creating monolithic character subclasses.

